<article class="env-definition" id="02NJ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02NJ">Definition <span data-tag="02NJ">29.30.1</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to S$ be a morphism of schemes. Assume $f$ is locally of finite type. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
We say $f$ is of <em>relative dimension $\leq d$ at $x$</em> if $\dim _ x(X_{f(x)}) \leq d$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
We say $f$ is of <em>relative dimension $\leq d$</em> if $\dim _ x(X_{f(x)}) \leq d$ for all $x \in X$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
We say $f$ is of <em>relative dimension $d$</em> if all nonempty fibres $X_ s$ are equidimensional of dimension $d$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>